body:
@ataraxus since you referred to the RHEL UBI: My current position is that anything in any version of nmap in any version of the RHEL UBI should be under the license Fedora now calls `LicenseRef-Nmap`. You may be aware that the upstream maintainer of Nmap has granted permission to use the old license (what Fedora now calls `LicenseRef-Nmap`) for certain releases licensed under certain versions of the Nmap Public Source License. There is an error (or at least, it is arguably an error) in certain versions of RHEL which I'll try to get fixed, wherein the nominal license in the package is the license Fedora now calls `LicenseRef-NPSL-0.93`. I say it is arguably an error because we intend not to ship anything in Fedora or CentOS Stream/RHEL under any version of the NPSL and we intend to use any permission given by upstream to stay on `LicenseRef-Nmap`, the pre-NPSL license. 

I realize this has nothing to do with whether any version of any Nmap license should be given an SPDX identifier. 

cc: @mosvald
